"Dari prakiraan ECMWF. FFMC = mudahnya serasah/rumput menyala; ISI = kecepatan menjalar; DC = kekeringan lapisan dalam & gambut; FWI = intensitas umum. Tingkat harian = kelas tertinggi FFMC/DC; bila BMKG dan ECMWF berbeda dipakai yang lebih tinggi.": "From the ECMWF forecast. FFMC = how easily litter/grass ignites; ISI = rate of spread; DC = drought of deep layers & peat; FWI = overall intensity. Daily level = highest FFMC/DC class; when BMKG and ECMWF differ, the higher one is used.",
"Prakiraan musiman · # bulan ke depan (ECMWF SEAS#)": "Seasonal forecast · next # months (ECMWF SEAS#)",
"Sumber: ECMWF SEAS# (sistem prakiraan musiman ECMWF/Copernicus C#S), # anggota ensemble, via Open-Meteo Seasonal API; normal = ERA# #–# di titik yang sama. Peluang dihitung dari jumlah anggota ensemble yang jatuh di bawah/di antara/di atas tersil normal ERA#. Belum dikoreksi bias model terhadap ERA#; gunakan sebagai kecenderungan dan bandingkan dengan Prakiraan Hujan Bulanan resmi BMKG. Prakiraan resmi BMKG:": "Source: ECMWF SEAS# (ECMWF/Copernicus C#S seasonal forecasting system), # ensemble members, via the Open-Meteo Seasonal API; normal = ERA# #–# at the same point. Probabilities are the share of ensemble members falling below/between/above the ERA# normal terciles. Not bias-corrected against ERA#; use it as a tendency and compare with the official BMKG Monthly Rainfall Forecast. Official BMKG forecast:",
"# titik panas": "# hotspots",
"Sumber: Open-Meteo Historical Weather API – reanalisis ECMWF ERA#/ERA#-Land (Copernicus Climate Change Service), titik # LU, # BT (Desa @). Reanalisis = model iklim yang menggabungkan pengamatan satelit & stasiun (grid ±#–# km), bukan alat ukur di desa. Data tersedia # § # – # § #. Normal = rata-rata tanggal yang sama tahun #–# (# tahun).": "Source: Open-Meteo Historical Weather API – ECMWF ERA#/ERA#-Land reanalysis (Copernicus Climate Change Service), point # N, # E (@ Village). Reanalysis = a climate model combining satellite & station observations (±#–# km grid), not a measurement in the village. Data available # § # – # § #. Normal = mean of the same dates in #–# (# years).",
"Hari #–#: BMKG + ECMWF (keyakinan tinggi) · hari #–#: ECMWF (sedang) · hari #–#: ECMWF, kecenderungan (rendah). Prakiraan dapat meleset; peringatan ini alat bantu kewaspadaan, bukan pengganti informasi resmi BMKG/Manggala Agni. Metode: Fire Weather Index (Van Wagner #) dari cuaca pukul #.# & hujan # jam, riwayat ERA# Copernicus # hari; ECMWF IFS #,#° (CC BY #).": "Days #–#: BMKG + ECMWF (high confidence) · days #–#: ECMWF (moderate) · days #–#: ECMWF, trend (low). Forecasts can be wrong; this warning is an aid to vigilance, not a substitute for official BMKG/Manggala Agni information. Method: Fire Weather Index (Van Wagner #) from #:# weather & # hour rainfall, ERA# Copernicus history of # days; ECMWF IFS #.#° (CC BY #).",
"Pembaruan otomatis & kesehatan data": "Automatic updates & data health",
